==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|baft}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|obaft}}, {{m|enm|baft}}, {{m|enm|baften}}, from {{der|en|ang|beæftan}}; {{m|ang|be||by}} (modern English {{m|en|by}}) + {{m|ang|æftan||behind}} (modern English {{m|en|after}}).<ref name=AHD>{{cite-book|editor=Morris, William|title=The American Heritage Dictionary of the English Language|year=1969|year_published=1971|publisher=American Heritage Publishing Co., Inc.|location=New York, NY|isbn=0-395-09066-0|page=1}}</ref><ref name=RH>{{cite-book|editor=Urdang, Laurence|title=The Random House College Dictionary|year=1975|year_published=1984|publisher=Random House, Inc.|location=New York, NY|isbn=0-394-43600-8|page=1}}</ref> See also {{m|en|aft}}.

