===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} On the [[aft]] side; in the [[stern]]. {{defdate|First attested in the early 17<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
#: {{ux|en|We drifted with the wind '''abaft'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The mate sleeps '''abaft'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1599|author=w:Nicholas Downton|chapter=The firing and sinking of the stout and warrelike Carack called ''Las Cinque Llaguas''|editor=w:Richard Hakluyt|title=The Principal Navigations, Voyages, Traffiques and Discoveries of the English Nation|location=London|section=Volume 2, Part 2, p. 200|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A02495.0001.001
|passage=The ''Exchange'' also being farther from the fire, afterward was more easily cleared, and fell off from '''abaft'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1785|author=John Rickman|title=Journal of {{w|James Cook|Captain Cook}}’s Last Voyage|location=London|publisher=E. Newbery|section=Part 1, p. 103|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/004895036.0001.000
|passage=By clapping the sails to the mast, and lightening the ship '''abaft''', we swayed her off with little damage.}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|page=452|chapter=[https://archive.org/details/mobydickorwhale01melv/page/452/mode/1up?q=abaft Chapter 95]|text=Stubb was struck by a shower of outcries and [[anathema]]s proceeding from the Captain’s round-house '''abaft''';}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1954|author=w:Aldous Huxley|title=w:The Doors of Perception|location=New York|publisher=Perennial|year_published=1970|page=72|url=https://archive.org/details/doorsofperceptio00huxl/page/72/mode/1up?q=abaft
|passage=We cover our anterior nakedness with some philosophy—Christian, Marxian, Freudo-Physicalist—but '''abaft''' we remain uncovered, at the mercy of the winds of circumstance.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|obsolete}} Backwards. {{defdate|Attested from around (1150 to 1350) until the late 15<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=2}}</ref>

